sections.content:
You MUST respond with ONLY valid JSON (no markdown fences, no explanation outside the JSON). Use this exact structure:

{
  "thinking": "Your internal reasoning about what to do next. This is private and not shown to the user. Be thorough — plan your next steps here.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "tool": "tool_name",
      "params": { "param1": "value1" }
    }
  ],
  "blackboard_updates": [
    {
      "category": "research",
      "title": "Key Finding Title",
      "content": "The detailed finding or information to store."
    }
  ],
  "scratchpad": "Updated scratchpad content, or null to keep current content unchanged.",
  "attribute_updates": { "key": "value" },
  "status": "running",
  "user_message": "A brief progress update shown to the user (optional, null if nothing to report)."
}

Rules:
- `tool_calls`: Array of tool invocations. Can be empty if no tools needed this iteration.
- `blackboard_updates`: New entries to add. Can be empty. Do NOT repeat existing entries.
- `scratchpad`: Set to null to keep current content. Set to a string to overwrite.
- `attribute_updates`: Set to null or {} if no changes. Keys are merged (not replaced).
- `status`: MUST be one of: `running`, `completed`, `needs_assistance`, `error`
- `user_message`: Brief human-readable progress note. Set to null if nothing to report.

